course: dictionary
lesson: 3244
title: Eons: very, very long times
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eon is an extremely long time, too long to count easily. Scientists also use eon for the biggest parts of Earth's history. «Earth's history is divided into eons, eras and periods, such as the Jurassic, about 200 to 145 million years ago, and the Cretaceous.» The order goes from biggest to smallest: eon, then era, then period.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «I waited for eons» does not mean you really waited billions of years. Eons here is an exaggeration, so it means a very long time, much longer than it felt. Always check: does the meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Eon is also spelled aeon in the UK, and the two spellings mean the same thing.
fact: An eon is the biggest division of Earth's history, lasting hundreds of millions of years or more.
fact: Eons are divided into eras, and eras are divided into periods. The Jurassic is a period.
fact: «Eons» in everyday talk means a very long time, as in «I waited for eons».
fact: The Phanerozoic eon is the eon we live in now, and it began more than 500 million years ago.
fact: UK spelling is aeon, but eon means the same thing.
exercise: «Earth's history is divided into eons, eras and periods.» In science, what is an eon? | A type of fossil | A tiny part of a day | A kind of rock | *The biggest division of Earth's history, lasting hundreds of millions of years or more
exercise: «I waited for eons» for the bus. What does eons mean here? | Two small rocks | *A very long time, much longer than it really felt | Exactly one hour | Very quickly
exercise: In «eons, eras and periods», which word names the biggest division of Earth's history? | period | *eon | era | fossil
test: Which is the bigger division of time, a period or an eon? | A period | Neither of them exists | They are the same size | *An eon
test: Grandma says she has waited for eons for her tea. What does she mean? | She ate her tea quickly | Her tea was cold | She waited exactly 1000 years | *It felt like a very long time
exam: Why is an eon much bigger than a period in Earth's history? | Because it is made of rock | Because it is kept in a museum | Because it is a shorter time | *Because it lasts hundreds of millions of years or more, much longer than a period
